   "parent_message_uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000"
  },
  {
   "uuid": "d2301de5-38ea-4d7d-9eae-646b219d6938",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-02-22T06:10:02.000000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-02-22T06:10:12.622000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Sidechain compression with Fruity Limiter is the standard way in FL:\n\n1. Route the **kick** to its own mixer track (say Insert 1) and the **sample** (Slicex) to another (Insert 2).\n2. Select the kick's insert, then right-click the arrow at the bottom of Insert 2 → **Sidechain to this track**. The kick now feeds Insert 2 as a sidechain without being heard there.\n3. On Insert 2, add **Fruity Limiter** → switch to **COMP** mode.\n4. Set the **SIDECHAIN** knob (bottom right) to 1.\n5. Start with: Threshold around −20 dB, Ratio 4:1–6:1, Attack ~1–5 ms, Release ~80–150 ms. Adjust until the sample dips just enough when the kick hits.\n\nFor lofi, a gentler duck usually sounds better than an EDM pump: aim for 2–4 dB of reduction.\n\nAlternative that's quicker: **Fruity Peak Controller** or a volume automation shape (or a plugin like a \"volume shaper\") linked to the kick timing. Less natural but very predictable.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
   "sender": "assistant",
   "index": 1,
   "created_at": "2026-02-22T06:10:12.622000Z",
   "updated_at": "2026-02-22T06:10:12.622000Z",
