  },
  {
   "uuid": "3ac301ad-dbc6-4edc-9c59-73ebfe6d42b5",
   "text": "",
   "content": [
    {
     "start_timestamp": "2026-02-22T06:11:52.622000Z",
     "stop_timestamp": "2026-02-22T06:12:04.056000Z",
     "type": "text",
     "text": "Do both, for different reasons:\n- **EQ the sample**: high-pass it around 100–150 Hz so its low end doesn't fight the bass at all. Soul samples often carry a lot of muddy low-mids; a small cut around 250–400 Hz helps too.\n- **Sidechain the bass** to the kick lightly (1–3 dB) so the kick punches through.\n\nUsually EQ'ing the sample fixes 80% of it; the sidechain is the polish.",
     "citations": []
    }
   ],
   "sender": "assistant",
   "index": 3,
   "created_at": "2026-02-22T06:12:04.056000Z",
